<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Cat care essentials</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Curious cat questions, answered.</h1>
        <p class="intro">
          A compact FAQ for new and seasoned cat people, covering everyday behavior,
          care basics, and ways to make home life more comfortable for your feline.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-card" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cat-mark">🐾</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-shell" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
      <aside class="summary-panel">
        <h2>Quick answers</h2>
        <p>Tap any question to expand the answer. Every section starts collapsed so you can browse at your own pace.</p>
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>8</strong>
          <span>common cat topics</span>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
            Why do cats purr?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed or content, but purring can also happen when they are stressed, healing, or asking for attention. Context, body language, and routine changes help explain what the purr means.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
            How often should I feed my cat?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Most adult cats do well with two measured meals per day, though kittens and cats with medical needs may require different schedules. Use your veterinarian's guidance and the food label to choose portions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
            Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead when they feel safe, are settling down for rest, or are marking a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
            Do indoor cats need enrichment?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Yes. Indoor cats benefit from daily play, scratching posts, window views, climbing spaces, puzzle feeders, and predictable routines. Enrichment helps reduce boredom and supports healthy instincts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
            How many litter boxes should I have?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>A helpful rule is one litter box per cat, plus one extra. Place boxes in quiet, accessible areas and scoop them daily so your cat has a clean and comfortable option.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-6" id="question-6">
            Why does my cat scratch furniture?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-6" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Scratching stretches muscles, maintains claws, relieves stress, and leaves scent marks. Offer sturdy scratching posts near favorite furniture and reward your cat for using them.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-7" id="question-7">
            Are hairballs normal?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-7" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Occasional hairballs can happen, especially in long-haired cats, but frequent vomiting is not something to ignore. Regular brushing can help, and repeated episodes should be discussed with a veterinarian.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-8" id="question-8">
            How can I tell if my cat is happy?
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-8" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Relaxed posture, slow blinking, gentle purring, playfulness, regular eating, grooming, and choosing to spend time near you are common signs of comfort. Sudden behavior changes may signal stress or illness.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    questions.forEach((question) => {
      question.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const details = document.getElementById(question.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
        const isExpanded = question.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        question.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        details.setAttribute("aria-hidden", String(isExpanded));
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
